# VentureOS Core

Portfolio OS for founders: ventures, kanban, financials, knowledge, calculators — multi-tenant via Supabase workspaces.

## Stack

- Next.js 16 App Router (RSC + client components)
- Supabase (Postgres + RLS + Google OAuth via `@supabase/ssr`)
- Tailwind CSS (dark theme: `ink-*`, `signal-*`, `fg-*`)

## Key paths

| Area | Location |
|------|----------|
| App routes | `src/app/(app)/` |
| Session / data | `src/lib/data.ts` → `getSession()` |
| Types | `src/lib/types.ts` (hand-written) |
| Supabase clients | `src/lib/supabase/server.ts`, `client.ts` |
| Auth gate | `proxy.ts` → `src/lib/supabase/middleware.ts` |
| Migrations | `supabase/migrations/` (numbered, run in order) |

## Conventions

- **Minimize scope** — smallest correct diff; match existing patterns.
- **No secrets in git** — use `.env.local`; never commit keys.
- **Workspace-scoped data** — always filter by `session.org.id`; never leak cross-org rows in UI even if RLS allows.
- **Server pages** that fetch live data: `export const dynamic = "force-dynamic"`.
- **Commits/PRs** — only when the user explicitly asks.
- **Supabase** — schema via migrations + `npm run supabase:db:push`; auth/Google via `config.toml` + `npm run supabase:config:push` (see `supabase-master` rule).

## Terminology

Use **workspace** in UI; **organization** (`organizations` table) in DB/SQL.
